WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.735
Our first guest tonight
is an 11-time

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.937
Grammy-winning musician
and one of the biggest stars

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:06.239
in the world.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.707
Her album,
"Red (Taylor's Version)"...

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:10.376
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-...is out tomorrow.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.812
She's also returning
to "SNL" this week

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.281
as musical guest along
with host Jonathan Majors.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.849
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.152
the one, the only...
Taylor Swift, everybody.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.354
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:30.997 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:40.606 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:42.709
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.143
-Thanks for having me back.

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:45.945
-We love having you
in the building, especially

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:49.315
when it means we get to see you
on "SNL" this coming Saturday.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.150
Your fifth time
as a musical guest.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.719
-Yes. What a dream.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.086
-And -- And a one-time host.

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:55.788
An incredible host
back in the day.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:57.156
-Thank you!

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:58.557
-And I'm wondering. You --
-Back when I was teen.

00:00:58.557 --> 00:00:59.892
-That's crazy
how young you were.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.293
-Yeah, I was -- Yeah.

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:03.129
-Because you're young now,
and that was a long time ago.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.164
-That is so -- Thank you.
-You're very welcome.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:07.700
I can say it honestly
because I've also aged.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.068
-What a -- What a friend.
No, you haven't.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.570
-Thank you very much.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.238
-That's -- Those are lies.
Don't say lies.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.539
-Having been a one-time --

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.475
and a first-time host,
obviously, when you hosted,

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.109
do you have any advice
for Jonathan,

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:19.045
your first-time host this week?

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:22.515
-Well, I -- I met him,
and I just want to say

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.817
he seems like one of
the coolest people on Earth.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.919
-Yeah.
-I think that everyone

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.688
needs to watch and just like --
He's amazing.

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:31.757
I mean, his work is
obviously so incredible,

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:33.860
and I'm a big fan,
but meeting him,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.528
you just get such a good --

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.630
Very real, very, like --

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.133
abnormally talented
normal personality.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.434
-Yes.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.403
-Those people
are unicorn-special.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.839
-Yes, it's so -- it's a very --
very nice combination.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.640
-Those are special,
special people.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.409
So, like, you know,
I -- I don't --

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.677
You know, what's weird
is I didn't get any advice

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:54.614
from anyone when I was hosting,

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:57.550
which is actually weird,
because I was like 19.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.684
-Yeah.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:01.220
-So I should've
been given advice.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.522
-Yeah. Real ball drop
on our -- our end.

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:04.691
-Right?
-Yeah.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.125
-There should have been,
like, a tip -- like --

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:08.895
like a number people call
to give me advice.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.529
But, no,
it's -- it's -- you know.

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:12.231
I think it's just
gonna be amazing.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.401
I'm so happy to get to be there,
to perform and to sing.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:19.939
You know, I -- I haven't played
with my band in years.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.275
And we're all like --
We all find it hard

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.610
not to, like, cry
that we get to play together.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.945
Like, we're all like,

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.780
"Did you guys make it through
that last pass?"

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.683
We're in rehearsals, just,
like, embarrassing ourselves.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.718
So it's just a dream
to get to do it.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.687
-Well, I think
it must be emotional

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:37.222
just to get back together,
but also, part of the emotion

00:02:37.222 --> 00:02:40.360
is you're singing songs from --
You know, you're re-recording.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.162
This is your second re-record.
-Yes.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:46.132
I feel like -- I know
that everybody has busy lives,

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:49.902
so I -- I do feel the need to,
like, explain what I'm doing

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.938
because it's not normal.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.539
-Yeah.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:56.742
-Basically, like, music --

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.311
I've always wanted
to own my own music

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.078
since I started making music,
and if --

00:03:00.078 --> 00:03:02.281
You probably don't know this,
but most of your favorite

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:05.218
artists do not own their work.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:09.521
The music industry is, uh --
Eh, you know?

00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:11.023
Certain corners of it.

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:13.325
But I think that there was --

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:18.197
There was something that
happened years ago where I --

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:19.732
I made it very clear

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.634
that I wanted to be able
to buy my music.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:24.236
That opportunity
was not given me,

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:26.172
and it was sold
to somebody else.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:29.808
And so I just figured, I was the
one who made this music first.

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:31.677
I can just make it again.

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:33.446
-Yeah.
-So that's what we're doing.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:34.947
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.784
-I have to say...

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.451
-So that's what we're doing.

00:03:39.451 --> 00:03:41.187
So when something says

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:44.290
"(Taylor's Version)"
next to it,

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.392
that means I own it,
which is exciting.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.661
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:52.231
-It's -- It's quite -- It's
quite a clever loophole, Taylor.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.133
-Oh, thank you.
-I really tip my cap.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.601
-Oh, thank you.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.971
It's -- You know, it's
also interesting to kind of

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:02.341
go back and relive
this nostalgia with fans

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:05.011
who are the reason
why I get to do this

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.746
and why I get to, like, sit here

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:09.782
and, like, have
this lovely chat with you.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.351
Going back and -- and reliving
these things with the fans.

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:14.953
And this time around,
I get to really --

00:04:14.953 --> 00:04:16.922
I get to do things
that I know they wish

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.257
I would have done
the first time.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.625
-That's really good.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:21.527
-Because I'm always listening
and I'm always lurking.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.028
And I'm always listening

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:25.197
to their opinions
and their theories.

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:26.866
And what --
You know, they'll -- they --

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.569
They will let me know which
songs should have been singles.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:31.771
-Yeah.
-They let me know which songs

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:35.074
did not get videos
and should have gotten videos!

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.076
And so I just like --
You know what?

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.411
Like, I'm listening

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:41.481
and I'm making the videos
and I'm doing the things.

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.348
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-That is really cool.

00:04:43.348 --> 00:04:47.486
I want to ask -- I mean, I have
emotional connections to songs

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:49.822
I listen to for the first time
ten years ago.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.724
I can only imagine
what it's like for you,

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.225
having written them.

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:56.996
Like, is it -- is it cathartic
to go back and re-record them?

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.298
Or does it -- When they're
about painful things,

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:01.200
do you, like, feel it
all over again?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.702
-I mean, I think -- for --

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:06.138
One thing that I noticed
about this --

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:08.073
just this week in general

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:12.578
is that I think back to
the release week of "Red,"

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.380
which is the album
that is, you know...

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.450
Just in case
anybody missed it.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.750
So this originally came out --

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.586
-This is it. It's this.
It's Taylor's Version.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.654
-Yeah, it came out originally
about a decade ago.

00:05:22.654 --> 00:05:28.628
And I was 22, and that release
week was so stressful

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:31.063
because nobody's heard
any of the music.

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:34.033
There are like 14 different
genre's on this album.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.803
It's a real patchwork quilt
of genre.

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:38.671
I was really experimenting.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:41.207
-A lot of 22-year-olds are going
to bounce around on genres.

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.876
-Hopefully. Yeah, you know.
That's what we want for them.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:46.412
-Absolutely.
-But I think that --

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:49.181
I was so focused on, like,
"Is anyone going to like it?"

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.449
And then I was also, like,

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:52.385
at the time, like,
honestly, really sad.

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:54.654
'Cause I had actually
gone through,

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:58.590
you know, the stuff
that I had sung about.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:01.660
But this time, I'm just like --
I got, like -- I have, like --

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.496
got sunglasses on
and, like, a mojito

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:07.232
and just like --
It's chill this time.

00:06:07.232 --> 00:06:10.569
It's really nice to be able to
put this album out and, like --

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:12.705
and not be sad, not be, like,

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:15.340
taking breaks in between
interviews to cry.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:18.444
It's very -- I'm telling you,
it's much better this way.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.579
-Yeah.
-Much better.

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.949
-We -- I think we're all happy.
-Yeah.

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:24.016
-With that said...

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.519
-You get some time passing,
you know?

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:28.520
-Yeah.
-You're -- You're reliving

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.957
your experience from your 20s
when you're in your 30s.

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.992
It's really the way to do it.
-Yeah.

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:35.961
I wonder if --
if there are people who might

00:06:35.961 --> 00:06:39.164
think that they were the one
you were singing about,

00:06:39.164 --> 00:06:43.268
if it's easier or far, far worse
for them ten years later.

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:45.371
-I haven't thought about their
experience, to be honest.

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:48.741
-I think that's the --
that's the biggest burn.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.042
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.544
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:54.980
I think there's nothing
they'd rather hear less.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.817
[ Laughs ] Hey. I have so many
more questions for you.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:00.520
We'll be right back with more
from Taylor Swift.

